coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder run [flags]

  Run a command on prepared template capacity

OPTIONS:
  -O, --org string, $CODER_ORGANIZATION
          Select which organization (uuid or name) to use.

      --cmd string
          Command to execute in the prepared environment. Required.

      --cpu string
          CPU quota as a positive whole number. Required; no template default is
          used.

      --env key=value
          Set a container environment variable as KEY=value. Repeat for multiple
          variables; the last value wins. Values are retained in admin-only run
          history.

  -i, --interactive bool
          Forward stdin to the workload.

      --ram string
          Memory as integer MiB or GiB, at least 16MiB. Required; no template
          default is used.

      --template string
          Template name or UUID. Required.

  -t, --tty bool
          Allocate a terminal and forward resize events. Requires --interactive
          and a local terminal. Terminal output combines stdout and stderr.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
